From: Bedrock for Mac contributors
Subject: winhttp: queue asynchronous writes issued from status callbacks

The bundled PlayFab SDK advances its send offset after WinHttpWriteData returns.
Inline WRITE_COMPLETE recursion from SENDREQUEST_COMPLETE therefore resends the
same body and corrupts the next request on the keep-alive connection. Queue such
writes on the existing request queue so the active callback unwinds first.

This is a compatibility workaround: Windows permits synchronous completion even
with WINHTTP_FLAG_ASYNC. Keep synchronous writes and async writes outside status
callbacks on their existing path.

--- a/dlls/winhttp/request.c
+++ b/dlls/winhttp/request.c
@@ -3653,7 +3653,9 @@ BOOL WINAPI WinHttpWriteData( HINTERNET hrequest, const void *buffer, DWORD to_write,
         return FALSE;
     }
 
-    if (!(async = request->connect->hdr.flags & WINHTTP_FLAG_ASYNC) || request->hdr.recursion_count <= RECURSION_LIMIT)
+    /* Let the active request callback unwind before completing another write.
+     * Some async callers advance their send offset after this function returns. */
+    if (!(async = request->connect->hdr.flags & WINHTTP_FLAG_ASYNC) || !request->hdr.recursion_count)
     {
         ret = write_data( request, buffer, to_write, written, async );
     }
